      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Cook the rice according to packet instructions. Keep warm with the lid on."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Make the gochujang sauce: mix 4 tbsp gochujang with 1 tbsp sesame oil, 1 tbsp sugar, 1 tbsp rice vinegar, and 2 tbsp water. Stir until smooth. Set aside."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Blanch the spinach in boiling salted water for 30 seconds, drain, squeeze out excess water, then toss with 1 tsp soy sauce, 1 tsp sesame oil, and a pinch of minced garlic."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Blanch the bean sprouts for 1 minute, drain, and season with 1 tsp soy sauce, 1 tsp sesame oil, and a little salt."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Stir-fry the carrot matchsticks in a little sesame oil over a high heat for 2 minutes. Season with a pinch of salt. Set aside."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Stir-fry the courgette for 2 minutes with a little sesame oil and salt. Stir-fry the mushrooms for 3 minutes with 1 tsp soy sauce. Set each aside separately."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Season the beef with 2 tbsp soy sauce, 1 tbsp sesame oil, and half the minced garlic. Stir-fry over a high heat for 3 to 4 minutes until cooked through."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Fry the eggs sunny-side up in a lightly oiled pan. The yolk should be runny."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Divide the warm rice between 4 bowls. Arrange the beef and each vegetable topping in separate sections around the rice. Place a fried egg in the centre. Scatter sesame seeds over and serve the gochujang sauce on the side."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "symptom": "Vegetables all taste the same",
              "cause": "They were cooked together or seasoned with the same amount of everything",
              "fix": "Cook each vegetable separately and season individually. Each one gets its own flavour before going into the bowl."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Rice sticks to the bowl",
              "cause": "The rice was left uncovered and dried out",
              "fix": "Keep the lid on the saucepan while you prepare the toppings. Use a small knob of butter or a drop of sesame oil stirred through before serving."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Gochujang sauce is too thick",
              "cause": "Not enough water added when mixing",
              "fix": "Add water a teaspoon at a time and stir. You want a sauce that drizzles easily, not a paste."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bibimbap is eaten all over Korea. It is a home meal. It is also a street food. The city of Jeonju is famous for it. Jeonju bibimbap uses raw beef and a hot stone bowl. At home, a regular bowl is fine. The dish uses up leftover vegetables well. It is a good weeknight option."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
